      "sourceTextSha256": "b38f7bb485344cea65041bbff99a67fbd71e05166359924e2413d1e1c338d5f9",
      "text": "This six-day route takes you from Mexico City and Teotihuacan to the ancient Maya cities of the Yucatán Peninsula. In the capital, you will see the Zócalo, the Cathedral and, if it is open, the National Palace with Diego Rivera's murals. The journey then continues via Villahermosa to Palenque, colonial Campeche, Uxmal, Mérida and Chichén Itzá.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "model": "ChatGPT",
        "runId": "ada-en-run-a40ee2cc",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The checked Word 2027 contains a route and detailed daily descriptions but no equivalent lead paragraph; translated the current RU summary, preserving its conditional National Palace visit."
      }
